.TH SOC-CTL 1 "October 2026" "OTA-Pulse" "OTA-Pulse Manual"
.SH NAME
soc-ctl \- control the OTA-Pulse monitoring daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soc-ctl
.I command
[\fIarguments\fR]
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the registration and service state.
.TP
.BI "config server " URL
Set the backend URL.
.TP
.BI "config token " TOKEN
Store the provisioning token (mode 0600).
.TP
.BI "config apikey " KEY
Store a device API key directly.
.TP
.BI "config deviceid " ID
Set the device identifier.
.TP
.B provision
Register the device with the stored provisioning token.
.TP
.B register
Register the device.
.TP
.B deregister
Deregister the device (see \fBsoc-deregister\fR(1)).
.TP
.B restart
Restart the monitoring daemon.
.TP
.B test
Test the connection to the backend.
.TP
.BR logs " [" \-f "|" \fIlines\fR "]"
Show or follow the daemon log.
.TP
.B help
Show the built-in help.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR socmond (1),
.BR soc-deregister (1)
